00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:22.011
- If you want to be successful
in starting a business,

00:04:22.011 --> 00:04:24.074
then you study what people have learned,

00:04:24.074 --> 00:04:25.672
and everything that people have learned,

00:04:25.672 --> 00:04:28.728
they've written down,
or shared in seminars

00:04:28.728 --> 00:04:31.390
or put onto audio programs.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:34.207
I learned this from a very wise man

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.889
named, Kopmeyer, who
spent more than 50 years

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:39.772
studying success, and he
had developed more than

00:04:39.772 --> 00:04:43.222
1,000 success principles
that he had derived

00:04:43.222 --> 00:04:45.738
out of something like 6,000 books,

00:04:45.738 --> 00:04:48.544
and when I met him, I asked
him the question you would ask,

00:04:48.544 --> 00:04:50.160
"Of all these thousand principles,"

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.751
'cause I had studied it all,

00:04:51.751 --> 00:04:54.677
"Which is the most important
principle of all?",

00:04:54.677 --> 00:04:57.034
and he said, "Brian",
he said, "It's simple."

00:04:57.034 --> 00:05:00.830
He said, "Use proven success methods."

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.682
He said, "Learn from the experts."

00:05:02.682 --> 00:05:05.036
He said, "Brian, you'll
never live long enough

00:05:05.036 --> 00:05:07.024
"to learn it all for yourself."

00:05:07.024 --> 00:05:08.946
So what I find, is that successful people

00:05:08.946 --> 00:05:10.665
are those who learn
from other's who've gone

00:05:10.665 --> 00:05:11.741
before them.

00:05:11.741 --> 00:05:14.032
Unsuccessful people try to make it all up.

00:05:14.032 --> 00:05:16.485
Like a cook going into the kitchen,

00:05:16.485 --> 00:05:18.398
taking ingredients out of the cubbard,

00:05:18.398 --> 00:05:20.285
throwing them all in a bowl,

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:22.283
and wondering why it doesn't taste good.

00:05:22.283 --> 00:05:23.957
This why people's sales careers,

00:05:23.957 --> 00:05:27.020
why 80 percent of
salespeople are functioning

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.490
well below their potential.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.485
Only 20 percent make all the money,

00:05:30.485 --> 00:05:32.498
why 20 percent of
businesses in any industry

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.989
make all the profits,

00:05:33.989 --> 00:05:37.542
why 20 percent of the
professionals in any service

00:05:37.542 --> 00:05:40.045
make 80 percent of the money, and so on,

00:05:40.045 --> 00:05:43.198
it's because they follow
proven success principles.

00:05:43.198 --> 00:05:47.434
Proven recipes, proven
formulas, proven combinations,

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:48.920
and they just do them over and over again,

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.190
until they master them.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.184
Then they can do more and more of them,

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:54.865
faster and faster, easier
and easier at a higher level

00:05:54.865 --> 00:05:57.071
of quality, and all that translates into

00:05:57.071 --> 00:05:57.985
greater results.

00:05:57.985 --> 00:05:59.662
- [Interviewer] Did not have
the rich dad in your life,

00:05:59.662 --> 00:06:01.935
what would you be doing today?

00:06:01.935 --> 00:06:03.668
- It's hard to say if I
didn't have my rich dad,

00:06:03.668 --> 00:06:07.085
because as a young kid, starting probably

00:06:08.489 --> 00:06:11.374
at the age of five,
six, seven, eight, nine,

00:06:11.374 --> 00:06:13.322
I really wanted to be rich.

00:06:13.322 --> 00:06:16.883
So I think number one is desire, you know,

00:06:16.883 --> 00:06:20.726
and then you naturally seek
your role models and teachers,

00:06:20.726 --> 00:06:23.972
and in my lifetime, I've
had multiple rich dads.

00:06:23.972 --> 00:06:25.944
You know, my rich dad was
my best friend's father,

00:06:25.944 --> 00:06:27.709
starting at the age of nine,

00:06:27.709 --> 00:06:30.840
and then today, I still
seek mentors and wise men

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:35.039
and wise women, because
that's how you get wiser,

00:06:35.039 --> 00:06:36.988
is by hanging out with smart people.

